From 26da04c8d52768f8f9b4dfd1b13a9e038b7ec267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:40:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: hand frames to the window system only once the GPU has
 drawn them

GameNative's window system takes no fence with a present. Its Vulkan
wrapper's X11 WSI sends the image to the X server right after
vkQueuePresentKHR has submitted (only MAILBOX waits for the GPU
first), and the X server draws the window from that AHardwareBuffer on
its next frame without waiting either; KGSL has no implicit sync
between the two processes. An image handed over before the GPU got to
the frame's copy into it is shown with what it held before: an older
frame, or part of one. In a D2R log with GPU-bound fights, every frame
was handed over ~0.5 ms after the game's Present() while the GPU
finished it ~41-44 ms later; calm scenes, where the frame cap held the
present, had the GPU ~5 ms ahead.

With VKD3D_FEX_PRESENT_DRAWN=1 the present waits, after the cap
pre-sleep and without holding the VkQueue, until the frame done thread
has seen the copy's fence (at most 200 ms), then calls
vkQueuePresentKHR. Frame start pacing measures against when the
present would have returned without that wait, so a frame the GPU
finished late still counts as late.

A new 'screen handoff' line counts the presents, those the GPU was not
done with when the queue thread was ready to present, and the wait
(also with the switch off, as frames handed over unfinished). The
present report flag 0x800 says the switch is on; the '# present:'
note says whether it applies.
---
